  "body": "Stacked on #1064 (base it on main once #1064 merges; it carries #1064's commits until then).\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed, per kind\n\n#904 left five kinds refused outright on any reduced-fidelity model. Same rule as #864/#904: a law gives the model's excess back out of its slack while a positive slack is left (`verify::excess_floor`); past that it reads untightened and the program gate refuses the op by name.\n\n- **Probe - now judged.** Both halves of the protected-move law read `probe_op::stylus_slack(excess)` = `STYLUS_SLACK` less the excess: the ball distance law (`stylus_hits_excess`) and the stem/body solid law (`stylus_reach_hits_excess`). The old functions forward with 0, so existing callers don't change. `generate` passes `material.excess`. Nothing else judges a probe against the model.\n- **Plasma - now judged.** The kerf law (part grown by `kerf/2 - tol`, which the lead planner reads too) and the cover law read `PlasmaParams::kerf_tol()` = `KERF_TOL` less the new `PlasmaParams::model_excess`. `plasma_op` fills that field from `material.excess`. The cut-order, crossing and tip-up laws read only the path.\n- **`fidelity_law`**: `excess_aware` now accepts Probe and every Plasma kind. `floor_of` also lists each kind's own slack (`own_law_tol_of`). `GOUGE_TOL` stays the base, so plasma is still refused at 0.01 mm of excess, which is stricter than its 0.025 mm law needs.\n- **Cone rides (2D chamfer, deburr) and engrave rides (trace, engrave) - still refused, with the reason recorded.** No law holds them to a tolerance against the model: the ride *is* the mesh edge by construction, so there's no tolerance to give back. Deburr also reads bends between coarse facets as creases. Judging them would need a new stated ride accuracy, which is open design, not a tightening. The reason is in `fidelity_law`'s header and the decision file.\n- **Cross drill - still refused; #1053 stays open for it (hence `Refs`).** Its part law and `rapids_radial` would each take a one-line tightening. But the chain is also proved by zero-slack readings of the mesh: `cross_stock::standoff` / `rapids_clear`, `cross_entry`, and `drill_reach`'s reach and holder faces. Tightening those means growing each measured standoff by the excess, which moves the kernel's stations. As #904 set, a law isn't tightened for a kind that stays refused.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/1053-fidelity-probe-plasma.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/coarse_probe_plasma.rs`. Each law is pinned so that a reading between the plain and the tightened slack is convicted only on the coarse model (excess 0.007), and a real hit is convicted on both:\n- `a_ball_between_the_slacks_is_a_gouge_only_on_the_coarse_model`: a touch 0.006 mm in; a real gouge at 0.05 mm.\n- `a_stem_between_the_slacks_is_a_shank_hit_only_on_the_coarse_model`: an overhang lip 0.006 mm into the stem; a real hit at 0.05 mm.\n- `the_probe_op_judges_with_its_models_excess`: the same lip through `GenerateOperation` on an import with no flag and one flagged 0.012 mm. This proves the wiring.\n- `a_kerf_between_the_tolerances_is_refused_only_on_the_coarse_model`: the part grown 0.02 mm past the cut outline; the kerf law refuses by name. A real reach at 0.1 mm is refused on both.\n- `the_stylus_slack_...` and `the_kerf_tolerance_gives_the_excess_back_and_reads_plain_past_the_bound`: past the bound the laws read their plain slack.\n- `probe_and_plasma_are_judged_while_a_tolerance_is_left_and_refused_by_name_past_it`, plus `coarse_laws::every_kind_is_either_judged_or_refused_for_a_stated_reason_on_a_reduced_model`, whose refused list loses Probe and PlasmaProfile: judged at 0.012 mm, refused by name at 0.030 mm.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/904-reduced-fidelity-laws`) and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` on the final head: green on 2e4058e7 (motion lib 31 s, 52 app suites 156 s, golden_cl plasma 1 s; 0 failed); clippy -D warnings clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The plasma cover law's tightening has no marginal pin. Its reading compares the path with the contour, and no fixture puts an edge between 0.018 and 0.025 mm past `kerf` on demand.\n- There's no document-level plasma fixture. The part region comes from the model's silhouette slice, which can't be grown by a chosen 0.02 mm, so the law is pinned through `plasma_profile`.\n- A bore touch on a coarse model: the tightened slack convicts a tangent touch once the excess passes ~0.0025 mm, because the bore's facets stand inside it. That's a false gouge on the safe side, the #1057 shape, and is recorded in the decision file.\n\nNo goldens or snapshots moved (`golden_cl::plasma_plate_with_holes_matches_golden` passes with `model_excess: 0.0`).\n\nChangelog: Probe and Plasma Profile operations can now post from a reduced-fidelity model (e.g. a metre-unit STEP file); their collision laws are tightened by the model's excess and refuse by name past it (#1053)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #1053\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
